    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `presigned_download.py` that generates a time-limited signed download URL for a stored object using a concrete external provider, I will use AWS S3 as the provider. This is because AWS S3 is a widely used service for storing and retrieving objects, and it provides a straightforward way to generate presigned URLs. The code will import the necessary AWS SDK (Boto3) and use it to generate the presigned URL. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789849489266,
          "start": 1789849486402
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
